1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
One sky. Belarusian farmers saw — a cart
in the stars.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Into the 21st century, researchers found
Belarusian village elders still knew the
star names.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:16,000
The Pole Star is Hvozdz, the Nail. The
whole sky turns around it.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Around the Nail turns a cart: the Big
Dipper is Voz, the Cart. The Little
Dipper is Maly voz, the Small Cart.

5
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:30,000
After Christianity arrived, the cart got
a driver: the prophet Elijah.

6
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:37,000
He never died: “a chariot of fire… and
Elijah went up by a whirlwind into
heaven.”

7
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:43,000
So the Big Dipper is also Illioŭ voz:
Elijah’s cart — a fiery chariot.

8
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:54,000
His feast day is in early August —
thunderstorms and harvest time.

9
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:59,000
Some think the driver was once the
Slavic thunder god Perun.

10
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:07,000
Not just Belarus: the Norse saw the
Man’s Chariot, Romania the Big Cart,
China the Sky Emperor’s chariot.

11
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Later in the evening, look northeast:
the Cart is climbing the sky.

12
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:18,000
Romania: a shepherd’s farm in the stars.
Follow for a new sky every week.

